          %title Spacetime
          %h2#Spacetime Spacetime
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+field+theory"} Relativistic field theory
            takes place on
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
          %p
            The concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            makes sense for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p+1
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in \mathbb{N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} observable universe
            has macroscopic dimension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3+1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            generally makes sense also in lower and in higher dimensions. For instance quantum field theory in dimension 0+1 is the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldline"}> worldline
            ” theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particles"} particles
            = succeed ";" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gt p+1
            may be “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+compactifications"}> KK-compactified
            ” to an “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"}> effective
            ” field theory in dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p+1
            which generally looks more complicated than its higher dimensional incarnation.
          %p
            However, every realistic field theory, and also most of the non-realistic field theories of interest, contain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+fields"} spinor fields
            such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
            (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LagrangianDensityForDiracField"}
            below) and the precise nature and behaviour of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinors"} spinors
            does depend sensitively on spacetime dimension. In fact the theory of relativistic spinors is mathematically most natural in just the following four spacetime dimensions:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AAAAA
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 2
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %mn 3
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %mn 5
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mn 9
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p +1 = \phantom{AAAAA} \array{ 2+1,\; &amp; 3+1,\; &amp; \, &amp;  5+1,\; &amp;\, &amp; \, &amp; \, &amp; \, 9+1 }
          %p In the literature one finds these four dimensions advertized for two superficially unrelated reasons:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                in precisely these dimensions “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistors"}> twistors
                ” exist (see
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a{:href => "twistor+space#TwistorSpace"} there
            %li
              %p
                in precisely these dimensions “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstrings"}> GS-superstrings
                ” exist (see
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes#TheSuperStringAndTheSuperMembrane"} there
          %p
            However, both these explanations have a common origin in something simpler and deeper: Spacetime in these dimensions appears from the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pauli+matrices"}> Pauli matrices
            ” with entries in the real
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebras"} normed division algebras
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+supersymmetry#SupersymmetryFromTheSuperpoint"} deeper still
          %p
            This we explain now, and then we use this to obtain a slick handle on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinors"} spinors
            in these dimensions, using simple
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
            over the four
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebras"} normed division algebras
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TwoComponentSpinorNotation"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TwoComponentSpinorNotation"}
            below).
          %p
            The relation between
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+spin+representations+and+division+algebras"} real spin representations and division algebras
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+supersymmetry#KugoTownsend82"} Kugo-Townsend 82
            %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+supersymmetry#Sudbery84"} Sudbery 84
            and others. We follow the streamlined discussion in
            %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+supersymmetry#BaezHuerta09"} Baez-Huerta 09
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+supersymmetry#BaezHuerta10"} Baez-Huerta 10
          %p
            A key extra structure that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinors"} spinors
            impose on the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            is its
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+structure"} causal structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/events"}> events
            ”) are in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/future"} future
            or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/past"} past
            of other points (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpacelikeTimelikeLightlike"}
            below). This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+structure"} causal structure
            will turn out to tightly control the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            in terms of the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+additivity"} causal additivity
            of the
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"} S-matrix
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TimeOrderedProductInducesPerturbativeSMatrix"}
            below) and the induced “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+locality"}> causal locality
            ” of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+quantum+observables"} algebra of quantum observables
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PerturbativeQuantumObservablesIsLocalnet"}
            below). To prepare the discussion of these constructions, we end this chapter with some basics on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+structure"} causal structure
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#RealDivisionAlgebras"} Real division algebras
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#MinkowskiSpacetimeInCriticalDimensions"} Spacetime in dimensions 3, 4, 6 and 10
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#LorentzGroupAndSpinGroup"} Lorentz group and Spin group
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#InTermsOfNormedDivisionAlgebraInDimension3To10"} Spinors in dimensions 3, 4, 6 and 10
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#CausalStructure"} Causal structure
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p#RealDivisionAlgebras
            %strong Real division algebras
          %p To amplify the following pattern and to fix our notation for algebra generators, recall these definitions:
          #TheComplexNumbers.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"}> complex numbers
                )
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generated
              from one generators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e_1\}
              subject to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} relation
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e_1)^2 = -1
                \.
          #TheQuaternions.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"}> quaternions
                )
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℍ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generated
              from three generators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e_1, e_2, e_3\}
              subject to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} relations
            %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 20px 10px 20px;"}
              %img{:alt => "quaternion multiplication table", :src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/QuaternionMultiplicationTable.jpg", :width => "300"}/
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi i
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 2
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e_i)^2 = -1
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,j,k)
                  a cyclic
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,2,3)
                  then
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi k
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_i e_j  = e_k
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi k
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_j e_i  = -e_k
            %blockquote
              %p
                (graphics grabbed from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+supersymmetry#Baez02"} Baez 02
          #TheOctonions.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"}> octonions
                )
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕆
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonassociative+algebra"} nonassociative algebra
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generated
              from seven generators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 7
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e_1, \cdots, e_7\}
              subject to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} relations
            %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 20px 10px 20px;"}
              %img{:alt => "octonion multiplication table", :src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/OctonionMultiplicationTable.jpg", :width => "400"}/
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi i
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 2
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e_i)^2 = -1
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi j
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_i \to e_j \to e_k
                  an edge or circle in the diagram shown (a labeled version of the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fano+plane"} Fano plane
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi k
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_i e_j  = e_k
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi j
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi e
                              %mi k
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_j e_i  = -e_k
                %p
                  and all relations obtained by cyclic
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
                  of the indices in these equations.
            %blockquote
              %p
                (graphics grabbed from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+supersymmetry#Baez02"} Baez 02
          %p One defines the following operations on these real algebras:
          #Conjugation.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (conjugation,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+part"} real part
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+part"} imaginary part
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+value"} absolute value
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℍ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝕆
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K} \in \{\mathbb{R}, \mathbb{C}, \mathbb{H}, \mathbb{O}\}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝕂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-)^\ast
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\mathbb{K}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbb{K}
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antihomomorphism"} antihomomorphism
              of real algebras
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi r
                            %mi a
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo *
                            %mo =
                            %mi r
                            %msup
                              %mi a
                              %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo ,
                            %mtext for
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi r
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi a
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi 𝕂
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mi b
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo *
                            %mo =
                            %msup
                              %mi b
                              %mo *
                            %msup
                              %mi a
                              %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo ,
                            %mtext for
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi b
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi 𝕂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    (r a)^\ast  = r a^\ast &amp;, \text{for}\;\; r \in \mathbb{R}, a \in \mathbb{K}
                    \\\
                    (a b)^\ast = b^\ast a^\ast &amp;,\text{for}\;\; a,b \in \mathbb{K}
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              given on the generators of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheComplexNumbers"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheQuaternions"}
              and def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheOctonions"}
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (e_i)^\ast = - e_i
                    \\,.
            %p
              This operation makes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
              into a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+algebra"} star algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              this is called
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+conjugation"} complex conjugation
              = succeed "." do
                %em conjugation
            %p Let then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Re
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Re \;\colon\; \mathbb{K} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Re
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Re(a) \;\coloneqq\; \tfrac{1}{2}(a + a^\ast)
            %p
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+part"}> real part
              ”) and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Im
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Im \;\colon\; \mathbb{K} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Im(a) \;\coloneqq \; \tfrac{1}{2}(a - a^\ast)
            %p
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+part"}> imaginary part
              ”).
            %p
              It follows that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝕂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \mathbb{K}
              then the product of a with its conjugate is in the real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/center"} center
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝕂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a a^\ast = a^\ast a \;\in \mathbb{R} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{K}
            %p
              and we write the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+root"} square root
              of this expression as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msqrt
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %msup
                          %mi a
                          %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert a\vert}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\sqrt{a a^\ast}
            %p
              called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
              or
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+value"} absolute value
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert -\vert}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\mathbb{K}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbb{R}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This norm operation clearly satisfies the following properties (for all
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝕂
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b \in \mathbb{K}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert a \vert \geq 0
                  ;
              %li
                %p
